  - should (optionally?) filter out TARGET/no.solo-words
  - should (optionally?) filter out DICT/reviewed.words?
  - should (always?) filter out DICT/no.words (which doesn't exist yet).

* dfs-anagrams: don't show dense cache details if dense cache isn't chosen
* -S 0 (auto) default (hardware threads)
* --require-completable auto
* -P 10000 default
* filter index entries containing configurable "skip words" during phase 1,
  especially `the`
* add -d/--dict option to top-segments, first-segments, filter-segments
* dfs-anagrams --wf -t FULLY-SCOPED-TARGET should infer -u from the target;
  currently it must still be supplied explicitly
* decide the BEST-pair bonus for dfs-anagrams invocations without -g; the
  dynamic scheme in plans/dynamic-best-bonus.md deliberately uses N from
  -g N and leaves the unbounded-search behavior unchanged for now
* dfs-anagrams --best-pairs probably should replace any implicit best.pairs
  inferred from --wf rather than being additive, and therefore should not be
  allowed more than once on the command line
* bring query-index scoring back into parity with dfs-anagrams (and the
  shared code planned in plans/rerank-anagrams.md):
  - fixed BEST scoring: candidate listing builds its DfsScoreModel with the
    fixed BEST exponent, since query-index has no -g, while dfs-anagrams -g N
    and query-index --score use descending BEST
  - additive --best-pairs: finalize_dfs_workflow_args still adds explicit
    --best-pairs to a full target's best.pairs for query-index, while
    rerank-anagrams replaces it
  - also: no workflow NO exclusions, index-only external pairs, and --score
    sums segments directly rather than with DfsTopN::emit's arithmetic, so
    exact scores can differ in the last bits
